                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4888ec1f-b580-3f53-88c2-e07524024ab6",
                                        "entry_id": "942f7849-20f2-3f65-b47a-8556fb36d502",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The emotional style of lyric poetry."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "271a9977-e093-3161-b97f-a33d0a32b0f1",
                                        "entry_id": "942f7849-20f2-3f65-b47a-8556fb36d502",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Suitability to be sung or used as lyrics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d5c13e2-0145-461e-a5ea-57914a28f5e8",
                                                "sense_id": "271a9977-e093-3161-b97f-a33d0a32b0f1",
                                                "text": "This is an album whose most memorable songs are definitely its strangest. Most ambitious of all perhaps is Dark Ballet, a long concept-song about Joan of Arc in which the lyricism of the piano lines startles. Madonna herself is heavily Auto-tuned, mumbling stuff about being a witch; she seems to blow on the flames of a pyre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29e02e48-2f4e-41dc-99ad-0c28d8df0dbb",
                        "source_entry_id": "a901c4f7-7f28-30cb-a64c-d3ecdf1b155c",
                        "target_lang_word": "lírica",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lírica",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bea4a780-605a-3407-91aa-43a681b9148b",
                                        "entry_id": "bdb20489-1f71-32a2-8c05-e011514a8f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Género literario dentro del cual se clasifican las obras que transmiten sentimientos personales y buscan generar una identificación emotiva, generalmente en forma de poesía y a menudo en primera persona. Tradicionalmente se opone a la épica y a la dramática."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a0aaa1f-54d6-4f1b-9e3d-b19744832408",
                                                "sense_id": "bea4a780-605a-3407-91aa-43a681b9148b",
                                                "text": "Épica y teatro son formas en las cuales el hombre se reconoce como colectividad o comunidad, en tanto que en la lírica se ve como individuo"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ea3f823-b5cd-3196-a19f-4cfbd041ddc5",
                                        "entry_id": "bdb20489-1f71-32a2-8c05-e011514a8f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Grupo de obras que pertenecen al género lírico₁."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83b00171-f06b-4c84-bf12-00fbcf98f6e8",
                                                "sense_id": "4ea3f823-b5cd-3196-a19f-4cfbd041ddc5",
                                                "text": "escribe mucha lírica auténticamente religiosa y amorosa"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5fa907fc-5c95-3832-b017-1c9068f7d4a5",
                                        "entry_id": "bdb20489-1f71-32a2-8c05-e011514a8f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Conjunto de la producción poética de una persona, grupo o época."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e11e5737-8172-4ba4-8e2b-19c451b4081e",
                                                "sense_id": "5fa907fc-5c95-3832-b017-1c9068f7d4a5",
                                                "text": "Pensamiento poético en la lírica inglesa"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8442d6af-56a5-386d-b4a8-d771ddac5fff",
                                        "entry_id": "bdb20489-1f71-32a2-8c05-e011514a8f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Por extensión, lenguaje que comparte características asociadas con la poesía lírica, especialmente el emotivo o sentimental."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce31e66b-afa3-41c3-95d0-3af310a285c1",
                                                "sense_id": "8442d6af-56a5-386d-b4a8-d771ddac5fff",
                                                "text": "Perdóneme la lírica, yo vivo en perpetua lírica infinitesimal"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"4\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
